          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Is FUNMILY a good treadmill brand?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              It is a budget brand with a website, a US address and a stated 12-month warranty, which is more than many marketplace names offer. But its website and Amazon listings give the same pads different motors and weight limits, and we found no hands-on review we could rely on, so judge each listing on its own.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Where can I find a FUNMILY treadmill manual?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              FUNMILY does not host manuals on its website. Look first in the “Product guides and documents” section of the Amazon listing you bought from, then ask the seller through Your Orders using the model number on the frame. Third-party sites index FUNMILY manuals by Amazon ASIN; check the model matches.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the weight limit of a FUNMILY walking pad?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              It depends on the model and the source. For the 12% incline handle-bar pad we found 300 lb on FUNMILY’s website, 350 lb on Amazon in May 2026 and 400 lb in a listing summary, and one indexed FUNMILY manual gives 100 kg, about 220 lb. Use the lowest figure for your exact model.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What warranty does FUNMILY give?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              FUNMILY’s FAQ says all its fitness equipment comes with a 12-month warranty for parts and labor, and that warranty details are on each Amazon product page. Support runs through Amazon’s Returns & Orders page or the phone number in the product manual.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Has there been a FUNMILY treadmill recall?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              We searched the CPSC recall database for FUNMILY by title and manufacturer on 5 November 2026 and found no recall. Check your model number on the CPSC site, since marketplace products are sometimes recorded under the importer’s name.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is a good alternative to a FUNMILY walking pad?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On 5 November 2026 the UREVO Strol 2E handle-bar pad was $169.99 at UREVO, with figures confirmed by two hands-on reviews. For an incline and a 400 lb rating that holds up, the MERACH NovaWalk W50 TrekPad was $299.99 at MERACH.
            </p>
          </details>
